namespace trion:
    use software

    section "The trion command converts":
        The trion command means the command that runs the trion processor.
        The language server means the command that serves an editor.
        A diagnostic means a message that the trion command reports about a package.
        The severity of a diagnostic is error, warning, or information.
        A conforming package means a package whose statements conform to the trion language.
        An output format means a format that the trion command writes.
        The output format of a document is MMT, Markdown, HTML, or an extension format.
        An extension format means an output format that a program outside the trion processor adds.
        A reading record means a record that states the meaning that the trion processor reads in a statement.

        [TOOL-CONVERT]
        When an author runs the trion command on a package P,
        the trion command shall follow this flow:
            step check: check the statements of P against the trion language;
            step expand: expand the composite sentences of P;
            step read: read the simple sentences of P as contracts;
            step write: write P in each requested output format;

            start check
            check -> expand
            expand -> read
            read -> write
            finish write

        [TOOL-EXIT]
        If a statement of a package does not conform to the trion language, then the trion command shall fail.

        [TOOL-DOC-CONFORMING]
        The trion command shall write a document of each conforming package when an author requests an output format.

        [TOOL-NO-PROOF]
        The trion command shall not prove a package.

        [TOOL-LSP]
        The language server shall report the diagnostics of each open source file to the editor.

    section "The trioc command proves":
        The trioc command means the command that proves the proof obligations of the MMT form of a package.
        A result means the answer of the trioc command for exactly one proof obligation.
        The verdict of a result is proved, refuted, or unproved.

        [TOOL-PROVE]
        When an author runs the trioc command on an MMT form M,
        the trioc command shall follow this flow:
            step read: read the proof obligations of M;
            step prove: decide each proof obligation of M;
            step certify: issue the requested certificates of the proved results;
            step report: report each result of M;

            start read
            read -> prove
            prove -> certify
            certify -> report
            finish report

        [TOOL-TRIOC-EXIT]
        If the verdict of a result is refuted or unproved, then the trioc command shall fail.
